<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs -Monday estimated 110,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs -Monday estimated 110,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog marketings Monday were 110,000 head, compared with 98,000 a week ago and no marketings reported on the Christmas holiday a year ago.  Estimates included generally about 60 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts sold $1.00 per cwt lower than midsession Friday. Trade was moderately active for light demand and moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				  Country		   Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    52.00 -53.00	   53.00 -54.00</p>
<p>few			51.50  53.50	   52.50  54.50</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    50.00 -53.00	   50.50 -54.00</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    46.50 -51.50	   47.00 -52.50</p>
<p>Sows: Steady to $2.00 lower.</p>
<p>US 1-3 300-450 lbs.  42.00 -43.00	   42.50 -44.00</p>
<p>450-500 lbs.	   44.00 -47.00	   45.00 -47.00</p>
<p>500 lbs. up	    48.00 -50.00	   49.00 -51.00</p>
<p>Note: Prices quoted represent sales of hogs averaging 73-74 pct. carcass yields with mostly 1.00-1.25 inches of last rib backfat and 47-48 pct lean. Special considerations and grade premiums not reflected in base prices.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
